  "note": "Election of the whole Coleraine Borough Council under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 16 October 1946 (not 18 September): five candidates for four aldermanic seats and thirteen for twelve councillorships; the results were declared on Thursday 17 October (Londonderry Sentinel, 19 October 1946, p. 6; Belfast News-Letter, 18 October 1946, p. 6). Nominations were received at the Town Hall on 1 October (Belfast News-Letter, 2 October 1946, p. 6). The queue's 18 September date is the Belfast county-borough poll; Coleraine polled later. Thirteen nominees for twelve councillorships. Seventy-five per cent. of the electorate of 3,532 voted. The nomination report prints John J. M'Candless and John H. Patterson; the result prints J. K. M'Candless and J. R. Patterson, which is followed here. Gribbon, the retiring member, was the only candidate defeated. Labour candidates were M'Laughlin and Neill. The four aldermen were elected on a separate aldermanic poll (see the Aldermen contest)."
